231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (Looking at Ondas' financial highlights, the company is clearly still in the growth and development stage rather than operating like a mature, consistently profitable business. Revenue came in at approximately $96.6 million, generating $43.5 million in gross profit, which shows the company is capable of generating meaningful sales and maintaining healthy margins on its products and services.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (The balance sheet is arguably the strongest part of the story. Ondas reported roughly $147 million in cash compared to only $22.7 million in total debt, giving the company significant financial flexibility. With more than $102 million in shareholder equity, the balance sheet appears well-capitalized and provides resources for future expansion, product development, and potential acquisitions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (On the other hand, the cash flow statement highlights the risks investors need to consider. Operating cash flow remained negative at approximately -$12 million, while free cash flow was even lower at around -$15.7 million. This indicates that the company is still spending more cash than it generates from its core operations. Capital expenditures of roughly $3.6 million further reflect management's continued investment in future growth initiatives.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
