/E (Unlike companies such as Ondas and Red Cat that primarily sell complete drone systems, UMAC is positioning itself as a supplier to the broader drone ecosystem and aims to benefit from increasing demand for domestically produced drone components. The company is currently focused on producing U.S.-made drone components, including motors, batteries, FPV systems, flight controllers, and other critical hardware used in commercial and defense drones. As for the stock's decline, I think much of it can be explained by expectations getting ahead of reality. UMAC experienced a massive run-up as investors became excited about the company's exposure to the growing drone and defense industries. In my opinion, the decline does not necessarily reflect a broken business model.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
